# .env file using Makefile variable syntax:

# How to fill this out:
# 0. Copy this file to .env.Makefile, and edit the values in that new file (not in .env.Makefile.example)
# 1. Open Finder
# 2. Menu Bar ➔ Go ➔ 🌐 Network  (Shortcut: ⌘ + ⇧ + K)
# 3. Find your NAS
# 4. the name of your NAS is the SERVER variable to fill below.
# 5. Double click it to open it
# 6. Find the shared folder you want to use
# 7. The name of the shared folder is the SHARE variable to fill below
# 8. Navigate to the folder where you want to put the zipped files
# 9. The path to that folder is the FOLDER variable to fill below
#    You can get the path by:
#      1. right-clicking the folder and selecting "Get Info"  (Shortcut: ⌘ + I),
#      2.1. right-clicking in the "Where" field (it displays the path separated with little ▸ arrows)
#      2.2. select "⧉ Copy as Pathname".
#      2. (Shortcut: double-click to select & ⌘ + C)
# 10. Fill in the values for SERVER, SHARE, and FOLDER (at the end of this file!!):
# 11. Save the file
# 12. Done, your `.env.Makefile` file is ready to be used with the Makefile.
#
# 13. Run `make` in the terminal to execute the Makefile with the filled-in variables
# 14. If you want to use a different file, pass it as a variable when running `make`, e.g., `make ENV_FILE=.env.Makefile.other`.

# Example:
# - Step 0: You opened your Terminal, wrote "cd ", dragged this folder into the terminal (Now says "cd /some/path"), Hit enter key (⏎), then typed "open -e .env.Makefile" and hit enter key (⏎) to open this file in TextEdit.
# - Steps 1-4: You opened Finder, Menu Bar ➔ Go ➔ 🌐 Network  (Shortcut: ⌘ + ⇧ + K), and found your NAS, named "YourNAS", so you fill in at the end of this file: "SERVER := YourNAS"
# - Steps 5-7: You double-clicked it to open it, found the shared folder you want to use, named "SharedFolderName", so you fill in at the end of this file: "SHARE := SharedFolderName"
# - Step 8: You navigated to the folder where you want to put the zipped files, up until you see the folder selected named "files" where you want to have the compressed application files archived inside.
# - Step 9: You get the path to that folder:
#           - Clicking the folder "files"
#           - Opening info, it shows  "Where: SharedFolderName ▸ folder ▸ path ▸ to ▸ where ▸ to ▸ put ▸ the ▸ zipped"
#           - Pasting it below in the file after "FOLDER := " will give you, for now: "FOLDER := SharedFolderName/folder/path/to/where/to/put/the/zipped"
#           - You'll need to remove the "SharedFolderName/" part, as that is SHARE: "FOLDER := folder/path/to/where/to/put/the/zipped"
#           - Now remember the name of the folder we looked up the Info on, "files",
#             and append it with a "/" at the end of the path for the final result: "FOLDER := folder/path/to/where/to/put/the/zipped/files"
# Step 10: Fill in the values for SERVER, SHARE, and FOLDER at the End of this file (not the next 6 lines!):
#     # Example for Server "YourNAS", and under "SharedFolderName ▸ folder ▸ path ▸ to ▸ where ▸ to ▸ put ▸ the ▸ zipped" the folder "files".
#     # Modify with your values:
#     SERVER := YourNAS
#     SHARE := SharedFolderName
#     FOLDER := folder/path/to/where/to/put/the/zipped/files
#


# Example for Server "YourNAS", and under "SharedFolderName ▸ folder ▸ path ▸ to ▸ where ▸ to ▸ put ▸ the ▸ zipped" the folder "files".
# Modify with your values:
SERVER := YourNAS
SHARE := SharedFolderName
FOLDER := folder/path/to/where/to/put/the/zipped/files

# Optional overrides (uncomment if the defaults don't work, e.g. `uv` is not found because make has a minimal $PATH):
# UV := /absolute/path/to/uv
# PYTHON := /absolute/path/to/python
